  {
   "id": "shevuot.6b.7",
   "daf": "6b",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "שְׂאֵת כְּצֶמֶר לָבָן. מַאי ״צֶמֶר לָבָן״? אָמַר רַב בִּיבִי אָמַר רַב אַסִּי: צֶמֶר נָקִי בֶּן יוֹמוֹ, שֶׁמְכַבְּנִין בּוֹ לְמֵילָת.",
   "en": "The mishna in Nega’im cited above states: «A se’et» is «like white wool.» The Gemara asks: «What» is meant by «white wool? Rav Beivai says» that «Rav Asi says:» It is the color of «clean wool» from a lamb «that» is «wrapped up [mekhabnin]» in a cover when it is «one day old» in order to protect it from being sullied, so that the wool will be suitable «for» producing «a fine wool» garment."
  }
 ],
